{"SurveyID":"SV_blu5q3SLhsOVeiW","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4483","SecondaryAttribute":"Aqueduct in the desert Settlements in the Burning Barren desert are supplied with water through a...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Aqueduct in the desert<\/b><br><br>\n\nSettlements in the Burning Barren desert are supplied with water through a series of aqueducts. The supply to Sandharbor settlement has been poisoned with Possuxyth, a potent, fast acting but relatively pain-free poison.\n<br> <br>\nThe people in Sandharbor will die if nothing is done. There are few options for relief efforts, as there are no off-road tanker trucks and any evacuation would take too much time because both communities are remote and inaccessible. However, the control engineer can remotely switch the supply to the Midcross settlement to Sandharbor. This would dilute the poison enough to make the water safe to drink, but kill the inhabitants of Midcross.\n<br> <br>\nYou are the control engineer. If you switch the supply from Midcross to Sandharbor, you will save 600 people in Sandharbor, but 30 people in Midcross will endure a painful death due to dehydration, which can take up to a week.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.desertAqueduct.vivid.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.600.n_total.630.n_victims.30.ratio_saved_victims.20.text","QuestionID":"QID4483","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Aqueduct in the desert Settlements in the Burning Barren desert are supplied with water through a...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
