{"SurveyID":"SV_blu5q3SLhsOVeiW","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4480","SecondaryAttribute":"Toxic factory A fire in a chemical factory threatens to release heptahopretyde, a gas that kills...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Toxic factory<\/b><br><br>\n\nA fire in a chemical factory threatens to release heptahopretyde, a gas that kills within seconds even in minimal doses. If released, everybody in the surrounding area will be killed, though the factory workers themselves will be fine due to their respiratory equipment.\n<br> <br>\nYou are the head of the firefighters. You can prevent the release of heptahopretyde by adding a chemical catalyst to the fire so the heptahopretyde splits up into harmless compounds. This will save 4,000 people in the immediately surrounding area. However, this will also increase the fire temperature, and 10 workers in the factory will die a painful death, being burned and asphyxiated alive.<br><br>\n\n","DataExportTag":"scenario.toxicFactory.vivid.counterbalancing_group.1.n_saved.4000.n_total.4010.n_victims.10.ratio_saved_victims.500.text","QuestionID":"QID4480","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Toxic factory A fire in a chemical factory threatens to release heptahopretyde, a gas that kills...","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},
